  "findings": [
    "resolve::resolve has no kernel/elaboration dependency and performs no type checking; its work includes macro and structure expansion.",
    "Elaboration namespace candidate comparisons can lower declarations and call kernel conversion. Inclusive namespace timings include those nested calls; exclusive groups avoid double-counting.",
    "The progress display previously stayed in Resolving while building the environment checkpoint plan; this work is now reported as Planning and measured as query.environment-plan.",
    "Dependency-filtered substitution keys preserve reuse across changes to unrelated module parameters.",
    "Provisional failed translations/comparisons are retained only within one candidate search and retried after materialization, registration or structural translation progress.",
    "Bounded kernel caches keep reused entries instead of flushing all entries; scratch lifetime validation remains active.",
    "The final Tensor check completed 11.46 percent faster; the selected DegreeZero check was effectively unchanged.",
    "The full differential_forms check still exceeded the configured memory limit during resolution, before query.resolve or query.check-batch completed."
